---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import checks from '../../../../../public/equipment/15-04/verification.json';
import m from '../../../../../public/equipment/15-04/interactions.json';
import {points} from '../../../../lib/equipment/15-04/solver.mjs';
const a='/equipment/15-04/',platform='https://noldus.com/shared/resources/book/noldus-product-documentation/chapter/ethovision-xt/page/ethovision-xt-19-welcome-to-ethovision-xt-video-tracking-with-ethovision-xt',ref='https://noldus.com/shared/resources/book/noldus-product-documentation/chapter/ethovision-xt/page/ethovision-xt-18-analysis-visualization-and-export';
const show=x=>typeof x==='string'?x:Object.entries(x??{}).map(([k,v])=>k+': '+(v===null?'—':typeof v==='object'?JSON.stringify(v):String(v))).join('; ');
const X=n=>55+12*n,Y=n=>252-12*n;
---
<Layout pageTitle="EthoVision XT context | Authored waypoint console" subtitle="" description="Step through an authored, nonbiological point diagram on an original 3D console, with explicit coordinate gaps." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment" id="wp"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/15-04/">← Equipment 15-04</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#wp-checks">Verification</a></nav>
<header><p class="eq-meta">15-04 / EthoVision XT software context / Offline geometric exhibit</p><h2>AUTHORED WAYPOINT CONSOLE</h2><p>Step through seven fixed drawing entries. Inspect each position and its displacement from the previous entry. When a point is missing, the display leaves the gap open instead of drawing a path across it.</p></header>
<div class="e-grid"><section class="e-card"><h3>01 · Inspect the illustrative workstation</h3><div id="wp-views" class="e-row">{['Bench','Screen','Keys','Rear'].map(k=><button type="button" data-view={k.toLowerCase()}>{k}</button>)}<button id="wp-xr" disabled type="button">VR unavailable</button></div><canvas id="wp-model" aria-label="Orbitable illustrative desk with an offline waypoint diagram and three keys"></canvas><p id="wp-asset" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><p class="e-hint">The white, teal and gold keys step back, step forward, and restore index&nbsp;1. Drag to orbit or pinch to zoom. The desk is original artwork, not a Noldus product.</p></section>
<section class="e-card"><h3>02 · Read a fixed entry</h3><div class="e-row"><button type="button" id="wp-prev">Previous</button><button type="button" id="wp-next">Next</button><button type="button" id="wp-reset">Restore</button><button type="button" class="e-run" id="wp-json">Export JSON</button></div>
<div id="wp-timeline" class="e-row" aria-label="Fixed timeline entries">{points.map((v,i)=><button type="button" data-index={i} aria-pressed={String(i===1)} aria-label={`Index ${i}, ${v.t} seconds${v.coordinateMm?'':', missing'}`}>{v.t}{!v.coordinateMm?' ×':''}</button>)}</div>
<p id="wp-status" role="status">Adjacent authored points</p><dl class="e-read"><div><dt id="wp-index">Index 1 / 6</dt><dd id="wp-time">0.5 s</dd></div><div><dt>Coordinate</dt><dd id="wp-coord">(3, 4) mm</dd></div><div><dt>Signed offset</dt><dd id="wp-delta">ΔX 3 mm · ΔY 4 mm</dd></div><div><dt>Length / interval</dt><dd id="wp-length">5 mm over 0.5 s</dd></div></dl>
<svg id="wp-diagram" viewBox="0 0 342 281" role="img" aria-label="Two disconnected sets of geometric points with a missing entry on the timeline">
<path d="M50 252h245M55 31v227" stroke="#829498" fill="none"/>{points.map((p,i)=>{const q=points[i-1]?.coordinateMm,v=p.coordinateMm;return q&&v?<line data-end={i} class={i===1?'active':''} x1={X(q.x)} y1={Y(q.y)} x2={X(v.x)} y2={Y(v.y)}/>:null;})}
{points.map((p,i)=>p.coordinateMm?<g data-index={i} class={i===1?'active':''}><circle cx={X(p.coordinateMm.x)} cy={Y(p.coordinateMm.y)} r="6"/><text x={X(p.coordinateMm.x)+9} y={Y(p.coordinateMm.y)-8}>{i}</text></g>:null)}
<text x="61" y="42" fill="#344f61" font-size="13">+Y</text><text x="280" y="245" fill="#344f61" font-size="13">+X</text><text x="66" y="272" fill="#344f61" font-size="13">Equal X/Y drawing scale · mm</text></svg></section></div>
<section id="wp-references"><h3>What this represents</h3><p>Noldus identifies <a href={platform}>EthoVision XT 19 as software</a>. Its <a href={ref}>EthoVision XT 18 visualization documentation</a> describes coordinate views alongside time views. These are context for this original exhibit, not a replication of either release or its interface.</p><div class="e-grid"><figure><img src={a+'original-front.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original metric workstation with a desk, monitor and keys"/><figcaption>Original geometry, not manufacturer CAD or imagery. The authored tabletop is 1,250 × 684 mm, with a 560 mm monitor bezel.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={a+'original-work.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original monitor, keyboard and three named display keys"/><figcaption>Original close-up. Keyboard, frame and monitor stand dimensions are authored design values, not a physical instrument specification.</figcaption></figure></div><p>All coordinates and time labels come from one immutable authored table. Offsets use the signed difference of adjacent points; length uses √(ΔX² + ΔY²). A missing point and the next available point both have no adjacent offset. No videos, camera images, live acquisition, arena, external trajectories, zones, or behavioral analysis are supported. The register’s zone-entry and acquisition acceptance is not implemented.</p></section>
<section id="wp-checks"><h3>Verification and files</h3><div class="e-over"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{checks.map(x=><tr><td>{x.id}</td><td>{show(x.expected)}</td><td>{show(x.actual)}</td><td>{x.pass?'Pass':'Fail'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p><a href={a+'reference-plan.json'}>Predeclared cases</a> · <a href={a+'verification.json'}>Verification data</a> · <a href={a+'authored-waypoints.csv'} download>Authored point table CSV</a> · <a href={a+'example-waypoint.json'}>Example JSON</a> · <a href={a+'waypoint-console.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={a+'geometry-source.mjs'}>Editable geometry</a> + <a href={a+'make-model.mjs'}>generator</a> + <a href={a+'mesh-writer.mjs'}>mesh writer</a> · <a href={a+'interactions.json'}>Named targets</a>. {m.triangles.toLocaleString()} triangles, {m.draws} draw primitives. Optional WebXR; physical headset untested.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/15-04/client.mjs';</script>
<style>
#wp header{max-width:73ch;padding:1.3rem 0}#wp h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,6vw,4rem);margin:.2rem 0}#wp section{margin:1rem 0}.e-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.e-card{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem;min-width:0}.e-card h3{margin:.3rem 0}.e-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.4rem;margin:.5rem 0}.e-fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.55rem}.e-fields label{display:grid;gap:.2rem}.e-fields input,#wp button{min-width:0;min-height:2.45rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:3px;background:var(--panel);color:var(--text);font:inherit;padding:.3rem .5rem;box-sizing:border-box}#wp button:disabled{opacity:.52}.e-run{background:#3d596e!important;color:white!important}#wp-model{width:100%;height:clamp(280px,34vw,440px);display:block;background:#ebe8e0;touch-action:none}#wp-timeline button[aria-pressed=true]{background:#3d596e;color:#fff}#wp .e-read{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.5rem;margin:.55rem 0 .8rem}#wp .e-read div{border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:.28rem}#wp .e-read dt{font-size:.85rem}#wp .e-read dd{margin-left:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere}#wp-diagram{display:block;width:min(100%,460px);height:auto;max-height:19rem;background:#ebe8de}#wp-diagram line{stroke:#566e7e;stroke-width:2.8}#wp-diagram line.active{stroke:#ae701f;stroke-width:4.6}#wp-diagram g[data-index]{cursor:pointer;fill:#375568;font-size:14px}#wp-diagram g.active circle{fill:#a4681c;stroke:#5d4727;stroke-width:2}
#wp #wp-references figure{margin:.4rem 0;min-width:0}
#wp #wp-references figure img{display:block;max-width:100%;height:auto}
#wp #wp-checks .e-over{max-width:100%;overflow-x:auto}
#wp #wp-checks th,#wp #wp-checks td{overflow-wrap:anywhere}
@media(max-width:720px){#wp .e-grid{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}}
</style>


